     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered the order. The FDA-approved sertraline label lists a maximum dose of 200 mg/day for adults, so 1000 mg is not within it. That holds across all approved indications: depression, OCD, panic disorder, PTSD, social anxiety disorder, and PMDD. I can't enter an order at five times the labeled maximum on that basis.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n\n- **Enter a dose within the labeled range**, such as 50, 100, or 200 mg once daily. Tell me which one.\n- **Review the label together.** The Dosage and Administration section of the current sertraline prescribing information gives the 200 mg/day ceiling.\n- **Involve pharmacy or the attending.** If you have a clinical reason to go above the label, such as a toxicology or psychiatry recommendation, the order should go through pharmacy review and be documented by the prescriber. I shouldn't place it directly.\n\nIf you meant a different dose or a typo, tell me and I'll enter it right away."
      }
